WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:06.960
British billionaire Richard Branson has big
plans for the Colombian border town of Cucuta.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.820
He says his goal is to raise money for food
and medical supplies AND ultimately get it

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:16.390
accross the border to Venezuela.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.670
Meanwhile everyday struggle for locals goes
on.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:23.360
Many cross the border here regularly to pick
up desperately needed supplies.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.340
They are hoping to see change soon.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.850
"We want to be free.

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:35.800
We want to be able to cross the border, we
want freedom, we want the government to fall.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.210
It is what we all want.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:47.030
And elections so we can have a new president."

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:52.289
Some however have lost all hope and are taking
extreme measures -- describing how it feels

00:00:52.289 --> 00:00:58.649
to be leaving their country for good.

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:03.659
"Right now I'm sad... this is degrading for
a human being.

00:01:03.659 --> 00:01:06.820
Very degrading."

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.260
President Nicolas Maduro is also taking exteme
measures.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.870
He sees any attempt to bring in aid as a pretext
for military intervention.

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:19.080
On Thursday he closed the country's border
with Brazil -- and said that he was also considering

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:23.210
closing the frontier with Colombia.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:31.480
"A complete closure of the border with Colombia,
I'm considering that.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:39.270
If it's best for a man to be prepared, it's
even better for a nation to be prepared."

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:43.350
That could make things tricky for Opposition
leader and self proclaimed President Juan

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.350
Guaido.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:50.659
He left his home in Caracas on Thursday to
make the 800 km journey to the Colombian border.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:55.460
He and thousands of his supporters are promising
to bring US aid into the country, but he has

00:01:55.460 --> 00:02:00.280
not explained how they plan to do it.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:04.510
Meanwhile back at the border just accross
the river from Cucuta, President Maduro is

00:02:04.510 --> 00:04:16.310
organising his own concert on

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:49.750
Venezuelan soil.

